      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "It wouldn't succeed if `A2` redirects to `B` which redirects to `A3`, as the TAO check is done in the `B` redirect response and would set the TAO failed flag. And it uses the [serialized request origin](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#serializing-a-request-origin) which takes redirect-tainting into account.\r\n\r\nAll of these concerns are baked into the TAO check already, all my patch does is ignore the `basic` [response tainting](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-request-response-tainting) when in a nested navigation.",
    "created_at": "2022-04-27T13:41:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-04-27T13:41:59Z",
